      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, `#define __ANDROID_API_V__ __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` could work. I think they wanted to use a concrete version numbers instead of 10000. Perhaps to support the case where two code names are under development. (with two different integers)..\n\n\n\u003e it would bake in the comparison against `__ANDROID_API_FUTURE__`\n\nI think this should be okay. `__builtin_available(android 10000,*)` becomes false on \"REL\" devices, which is what we want.",
